     5	which is an index derived from it. Every verification surface before this
     6	module walked the *index* only, so an out-of-band sqlite row — a row the log
     7	never carried — still rendered ``✓ chain intact`` at rc=0. That is a false
     8	attestation of exactly the lie-class the chain exists to prevent
     9	(design/store/verify-canonical-agreement).
    10	
    11	This module is the reader that judges the two artifacts against each other.
    12	
    13	**Pure reader, by contract.** Nothing here constructs a :class:`~engine.
    14	jsonl_store.JsonlStore`. That constructor *repairs* — catch-up, torn-line
    15	truncation, rebuild-on-divergence — and repair destroys the evidence
    16	verification exists to inspect. Open-time recovery and verification are
    17	opposite contracts, so they never share a code path: the log is read with
    18	plain file IO through :mod:`engine.jsonl_codec`, the index with a read-only
    19	sqlite connection, and neither offset nor count marker is ever written.
    20	
    21	Two depths:
