     1	"""Witness positions — the read-path temporal cursor (SPEC §9.3, 0.8.0 session 1).
     2	
     3	A cursor denotes the **inclusive witness prefix** of rows a store had received at
     4	a position: ``WHERE rowid <= resolved``. The selected prefix — domain facts and
     5	self-lineage ``_decl.*`` rows alike — is then replayed in ``(ts, id)`` order, and
     6	ontology resolves from the ``_decl`` rows *in the same prefix* (equal cursors ⇒
     7	same position for selection and ontology). This is the "what a reader at P could
     8	have seen" honesty of §9.3: late arrivals (merge / import / backdate) do not
     9	rewrite what an earlier position shows, because a backdated fact lands at a
    10	*later* witness position even though it sorts early under ``(ts, id)`` replay.
    11	
    12	Contrast with the shipped ``as_of`` event-time projection (``ts <= T``): that is
    13	an explicitly-requested analytical mode, never the cursor default. The two
    14	selectors are **mutually exclusive** (A8): a read is either witness-cursor'd or
    15	event-time-projected, never a chimera of both.
    16	
    17	Design invariants this module pins:
    18	
    19	- **Identity is a fact id, resolved by primary-key lookup ONLY** (A3). Ids are
    20	  never ordered or parsed for cursor purposes — the corpus mixes uuid4-era and
    21	  ULID-era ids, and even pure-ULID stores are not within-millisecond monotonic
    22	  (see :func:`~engine.sqlite_store.gen_id`). ``id -> rowid`` is a ``WHERE id = ?``
    23	  point lookup; ``rowid`` (append order) is the witness axis.
    24	
    25	- **Facts-only axis** (A1). Facts and ticks occupy separate rowid domains with no
    26	  durable cross-table receipt log in 0.8.0; the fold boundary needs only the
    27	  facts axis (ticks never feed fold state). A store-wide receipt ordinal
    28	  (GlobalReceiptPosition) is a queued protocol amendment, not smuggled in here.
    29	
    30	- **Receipt-group atomicity** (A2). An absorb-edit ceremony writes multiple
    31	  ``_decl.*`` rows atomically — one ``BEGIN IMMEDIATE``, one stamped effective
    32	  ``ts``, contiguous rowids (``sqlite_store.absorb_edit``). A cursor that lands
    33	  *strictly inside* such a group would select a half-applied ceremony, so
    34	  resolution **refuses on ambiguity** (:class:`MidReceiptGroupPosition`) rather
    35	  than silently folding a partial ontology. The guard lives at the engine
    36	  selector — every ``at=`` seam runs it — not only in the CLI address resolver.
    37	  In 0.8.0 the group boundary is a *heuristic* (contiguity + shared ts + shared
    38	  lineage), origin-guaranteed by the write path but not interchange-guaranteed;
    39	  a durable group id is a queued protocol amendment.
    40	
    41	- **Unadopted stores** (N1). The live corpus is overwhelmingly pre-genesis: no
    42	  ``_decl.genesis``, no ``store_meta.own_lineage`` marker, so nothing to qualify
    43	  a durable handle with. In-session positions work everywhere, but a cursor
    44	  against an unadopted store carries :attr:`WitnessPosition.unadopted` — durable
