   287	    :func:`resolve_cut_summary`, 0.9.0 S6 sol P1) can share one connection/
   288	    transaction instead of paying ``resolve_witness_position``'s own
   289	    open-resolve-close per call — each such call is otherwise a separate
   290	    WAL snapshot, so a concurrent writer's commit landing between two calls
   291	    would make the second describe a LATER store state than the first, a
   292	    silent internal race. ``store_path`` is used only to stamp
   293	    ``WitnessPosition.store`` (the position's home store, read by
   294	    ``verify_position_for_store``'s cross-store guard) — no I/O against it
   295	    here; all reads go through ``conn``.
   296	    """
   297	    fact_id, rowid = _resolve_address_rowid(conn, address)
   298	    span = None if group_boundary == "allow" else receipt_group_span(conn, rowid)
   299	    if span is not None:
   300	        if group_boundary == "floor":
