   334	    *,
   335	    timeout: float = 5.0,
   336	    anchor: TickAnchor | None = None,
   337	    group_boundary: str = "refuse",
   338	) -> WitnessPosition:
   339	    """Resolve a witness address to a :class:`WitnessPosition` against one store.
   340	
   341	    Address forms handled at this engine seam:
   342	
   343	    - ``"head"`` — the newest received fact, captured atomically (frozen once
   344	      returned; no moving token). An empty store resolves to the empty prefix.
   345	    - :data:`GENESIS_SENTINEL` (``""``) — the empty / start-of-store position.
   346	    - a full, canonical fact id — resolved by **primary-key lookup only** (A3);
   347	      an unknown id raises :class:`UnknownWitnessHandle`. Prefix expansion and
   348	      ``seq:``/``tick:``/wall-clock address forms are CLI-layer resolutions that
   349	      produce a fact id (or a rowid) to hand here.
   350	
   351	    Runs the receipt-group guard (A2) — a mid-ceremony position raises
   352	    :class:`MidReceiptGroupPosition`. Reads the ``own_lineage`` marker to set
   353	    :attr:`WitnessPosition.unadopted` (N1).
   354	
   355	    ``anchor``: for a ``tick:``/wall-clock address, the CALLER already knows the
   356	    exact tick it snapped to (from :func:`resolve_tick_cursor` /
   357	    :func:`resolve_tick_floor`) and passes it here so it is PRESERVED as the
   358	    position's :attr:`~WitnessPosition.anchor` (review finding 7a). Re-deriving
   359	    it from the cursor would be wrong when several ticks seal the same
   360	    ``fact_cursor`` — one of them possibly *after* the requested mark — and the
   361	    re-derivation would name that later tick instead of the floor tick actually
   362	    selected. When ``None`` (head/seq/fact forms), the anchor is derived as the
   363	    last sealed tick at-or-before the position.
   364	
   365	    ``group_boundary`` governs a position that lands inside an atomic receipt
   366	    group (A2). ``"refuse"`` (default, for exact forms — ``fact:``/``seq:``)
   367	    raises :class:`MidReceiptGroupPosition`. ``"floor"`` (for floor-derived
   368	    forms — ``tick:``/wall-clock, chosen by the CLI resolver per address form)
   369	    **snaps** to the position just before the ceremony's first row — the last
   370	    complete ontology state — rather than refusing (M3). ``head`` never lands
   371	    mid-group (a completed ceremony committed atomically). ``"allow"`` skips
