   806	            # calls unindexed already has its row. Same class as the
   807	            # ``_prefix_intact`` failure one line up in ``catch_up`` — the
   808	            # index is not a function of the log at the stamped offset — and
   809	            # the same answer, rebuild, because every colliding row IS
   810	            # reproducible from the canonical log (unlike the out-of-band rows
   811	            # ``_refuse_out_of_band`` protects). Raising instead would make the
   812	            # store a permanent dead end that the verify gate calls
   813	            # recoverable; before this, it surfaced as a raw sqlite
   814	            # IntegrityError traceback out of every read verb.
   815	            self._conn.rollback()
