   823	    def _rebuild(self, reason: str) -> None:
   824	        """Rebuild the whole sqlite index from the log.
   825	
   826	        Clears ``facts`` and ``ticks`` only: ``store_meta`` survives, because
   827	        ``own_lineage`` (which ``_decl.genesis`` row is *self*) is identity,
   828	        not fact — it is not in the log and cannot be re-derived from it.
   829	
   830	        The FTS index is dropped in the same transaction. ``facts`` has no
   831	        ``AUTOINCREMENT``, so ``DELETE FROM facts`` resets sqlite's rowid
   832	        counter and re-indexed rows take rowids that previously named other
   833	        facts. ``facts_fts.fact_rowid`` keys on exactly that rowid and
   834	        ``fts_state.last_rowid`` is the incremental watermark, so a surviving
   835	        FTS index would resolve stale text to new facts and skip every
   836	        re-indexed row. Dropping it makes search report ``missing`` (the
   837	        honest "run reindex" state) instead of answering wrongly.
