   668	    def absorb_genesis(
   669	        self,
   670	        documents: list,
   671	        *,
   672	        observer: str,
   673	        origin: str = "",
   674	        fact_signer: Callable[[str, str], str | None] | None,
   675	        protocol: int | None = None,
   676	    ) -> dict[str, Any]:
   677	        """Open the store's declaration lineage — the atomic genesis primitive.
   678	
   679	        The lineage-opening ceremony's write half (SPEC §9.2 era rule),
   680	        performed as ONE ``BEGIN IMMEDIATE`` transaction so the identity check,
   681	        the era pins, and the append are indivisible: a concurrent emit cannot
   682	        falsify a pin between read and write, and two concurrent absorbs cannot
   683	        both mint a genesis (the second blocks on the write lock, then sees the
   684	        first's row and refuses).
   685	
   686	        Steps, all inside the transaction:
   687	
   688	        1. Refuse (``GenesisExists``) if the store's OWN lineage is already
   689	           open — the ``store_meta.own_lineage`` marker exists. An unmarked
   690	           store with ANY ``_decl.genesis`` rows refuses as ambiguous:
   691	           identity is claimed only by the explicit :meth:`adopt_lineage`
   692	           ceremony, never inferred from facts (the singleton heuristic was
   693	           a hijack vector — closing re-review #1). Foreign genesis rows
   694	           (marker present, ids differ) do NOT block: merge legitimately
   695	           carries them as inert citizens (§9.2 Lineage), and a store that
   696	           received one must still be able to mint its own identity.
   697	        2. Read the era pins — chain head (latest chained tick's row hash) and
   698	           fact cursor (newest fact by WITNESS order / rowid) — so
   699	           "everything before me predates historization" is verifiable.
   700	        3. Build the whole payload (``documents`` + ``protocol`` + pins), sign
   701	           its CONTENT commitment under ``observer`` via ``fact_signer``, and
   702	           refuse (``UnsignableGenesis``, rollback) if no signature is
   703	           produced. The signed commitment is over the ACTUAL final payload,
   704	           never a throwaway probe — genesis is the attestation root.
   705	        4. Append the ``_decl.genesis`` row, stamp ``store_meta.own_lineage``
   706	           with its id (the store-local identity marker — merge copies facts,
   707	           never meta, so identity cannot arrive from outside), and commit.
   708	           The genesis row's own id IS the lineage id (§9.2), returned in the
   709	           receipt.
