   823	        """Re-emit changed declaration subjects over an open lineage (S4).
   824	
   825	        The edit ceremony's write half (SPEC §9.2). Each ``change`` is a
   826	        subject-granular whole-document delta (from
   827	        ``lang.document.diff_documents``), duck-typed by four attributes:
   828	        ``kind`` (the final ``_decl.*-defined`` or ``*-retired`` event kind),
   829	        ``subject``, ``payload`` (the whole document payload for a definition,
   830	        ``None`` for a removal), and ``annotation`` (``added``/``modified``/
   831	        ``removed`` — rides the row as ``change=``).
   832	
   833	        Performed as ONE ``BEGIN IMMEDIATE`` transaction so the batch is
   834	        all-or-nothing (a half-applied ontology change is the §9.1 lie
   835	        mid-flight) and the lineage id is read consistently:
   836	
   837	        1. Resolve the store's OWN lineage: the ``store_meta.own_lineage``
   838	           marker. No marker + no genesis rows → :class:`NoGenesis`;
   839	           unmarked + genesis rows → :class:`AmbiguousGenesis` (identity is
   840	           claimed by :meth:`adopt_lineage`, never inferred).
