Two contract gaps have emerged from code tracing and are now queued for empirical confirmation: the public KDL mutation API deliberately refuses single-line edit/remove and per-kind parse serialization despite the primary contract requiring those shapes, and the declaration intent file is published by replacement rather than exclusive creation, leaving a same-head concurrent-apply race. I’m continuing through tests and constructing deterministic reproductions before assigning severity.
Contract mapping is complete; implementation inspection found candidate gaps that need empirical reproduction.
