    30	  `GenesisExists`) / `refused` / `pending-intent` / `needs-recovery`.
    31	  Signing rides the ratified S3 `CredentialProvider` shape.
    32	- **File-cache replacement** — the recommended store-first shape shipped as
    33	  the default: atomic (tempfile + fsync + rename) replace of the `.vertex`
    34	  with the proposed source text, byte-preserving the author's presentation.
    35	  The step is injectable (`write_file=`), which doubles as the oracle-3 kill
    36	  seam.
    37	- **`recover_declaration_update(intent_path)`** — idempotent, classifies
    38	  from fingerprint evidence, never guesses: store projection == proposed →
    39	  `already-applied` (file matches) or `safe-to-finish` (completes the file
    40	  replace, clears the intent); == pre-ceremony state → `not-applied`
    41	  (intent void, discarded); anything else → `conflict` (intent AND file
    42	  left untouched). Second recover after a finish is an `already-applied`
    43	  no-op. Corrupt intent → `IntentCorrupt`, refuses loudly, nothing deleted.
    44	
    45	## Design decisions (judgment fences exercised)
    46	
    47	- **Free functions, not VertexHandle methods.** VertexHandle is a held
    48	  live read/receive session (lock, cursors, snapshots); a declaration
    49	  ceremony is a one-shot operation keyed on a vertex path. `open_vertex`
    50	  is the composition precedent for path-keyed free functions in
    51	  `engine.handle`; `ceremony.py` follows it.
    52	  (decision:architecture/ceremony-orchestration-free-functions)
    53	- **Intent placement: sibling `<name>.vertex.intent`.** (a) the vertex path
    54	  is the one handle plan, apply, and recover all share; (b) a
    55	  JSONL-canonical store has TWO adjacent artifacts (log + index) with no
    56	  single obvious slot; (c) the store locator is exactly what a ceremony may
    57	  be mid-edit on — the file being reconciled is the stable coordinate.
    58	  Survives process death; discoverable via `intent_path_for(vertex_path)`.
    59	  Pending intent blocks new plan/apply (typed) — that is what makes
    60	  `conflict` non-lossy.
    61	- **Order-independent fingerprints.** Applied-detection hashes documents
    62	  sorted by `(kind, subject)`. Deliberately NOT `declaration_generation`'s
    63	  review fingerprint (order-sensitive, same-source comparator): the file
    64	  projects documents in declaration order while the store fold appends
    65	  added subjects, so an order-sensitive hash would misclassify a committed
    66	  ceremony as `conflict` after a mid-file add.
    67	
    68	## Deviations / findings
    69	
    70	1. **Fourth recovery class `not-applied`** (extension of the task's three):
    71	   store-first ordering makes "intent durable, store never committed"
    72	   reachable; folding it into `conflict` or `safe-to-finish` would be a
    73	   guess. (observation:implementation/s2-recovery-not-applied-class)
    74	2. **Index-loss recovery requires explicit adoption.** A rebuilt index has
    75	   no `own_lineage` marker (S1b anti-hijack ratchet — identity adopted,
    76	   never inferred), so recovery over a lost index surfaces
    77	   `UnadoptedLineage`; `adopt_lineage()` then recover completes. Pinned in
    78	   `test_recover_after_index_loss_classifies_from_the_log`. Not a blocker —
    79	   the honest behavior given the ratchet.
    80	   (observation:implementation/s2-index-loss-recovery-needs-adoption)
    81	3. **AST-only plans** (no `proposed_text`) mark the default file step
    82	   unavailable; a `safe-to-finish` over such an intent reports
    83	   `finished=False` with a disclosed reason rather than inventing KDL text
    84	   — presentation policy stays app-injected, per the contract's option.
    85	4. **CLI not migrated.** `apps/loops` `_absorb_*` still assembles the
    86	   protocol itself (its output is golden-locked); migrating it onto this
    87	   API is the intended forcing-consumer follow-up slice — sequenced scope,
    88	   not dropped scope. The loops suite passes untouched.
    89	5. Unadopted-store edge: a store with genesis rows but no marker plans as
    90	   `genesis` mode and refuses at apply (`AmbiguousGenesis` → `refused`,
    91	   adopt first) — plan never infers identity.
